{"file": "D:\\SpaceBook\\Books\\6th\\Math\\JPG\\092.jpg", "lines": [{"text": "per ticket?", "conf": 0.736, "box": [[209, 157], [375, 152], [376, 189], [210, 193]]}, {"text": "is the per square meter rate of tiling?", "conf": 0.936, "box": [[202, 263], [793, 258], [793, 300], [203, 306]]}, {"text": "Dania bought 12 kg of apples in Rs 720. Find the rate of 1 kg of apples.", "conf": 0.957, "box": [[197, 321], [1358, 293], [1360, 348], [198, 376]]}, {"text": "Aleem's income is Rs 3000 after working for 19 hours. What is his per hour pay?", "conf": 0.938, "box": [[196, 393], [1513, 360], [1514, 415], [197, 447]]}, {"text": "Think Higher", "conf": 0.844, "box": [[138, 488], [328, 490], [327, 524], [137, 521]]}, {"text": "Colour the following shapes and show that 0.5 is not equal to 5%.", "conf": 0.954, "box": [[195, 563], [1020, 553], [1021, 592], [196, 602]]}, {"text": "0.5", "conf": 0.692, "box": [[527, 987], [574, 987], [574, 1023], [527, 1023]]}, {"text": "5%", "conf": 0.654, "box": [[976, 991], [1023, 991], [1023, 1023], [976, 1023]]}, {"text": "According to a criterion, for every 6 square metre of area, the garden should have 4 plants. A garden", "conf": 0.929, "box": [[188, 1046], [1493, 1053], [1492, 1089], [187, 1082]]}, {"text": "that has an area of 54 square metre has 32 plants. Is the number of trees is correct according to the set", "conf": 0.914, "box": [[188, 1093], [1540, 1105], [1539, 1141], [187, 1129]]}, {"text": "criterion? Justifyyouranswer.", "conf": 0.914, "box": [[192, 1142], [557, 1150], [556, 1180], [191, 1172]]}, {"text": "Summary", "conf": 0.814, "box": [[132, 1229], [326, 1239], [324, 1276], [130, 1265]]}, {"text": "Vocabulary", "conf": 0.861, "box": [[1119, 1251], [1349, 1260], [1347, 1303], [1117, 1294]]}, {"text": "Percent", "conf": 0.822, "box": [[1086, 1326], [1196, 1330], [1195, 1364], [1085, 1360]]}, {"text": "Percent (%) means out of 100.", "conf": 0.856, "box": [[218, 1358], [687, 1368], [686, 1404], [217, 1394]]}, {"text": "Percentage", "conf": 0.826, "box": [[1089, 1378], [1242, 1385], [1241, 1416], [1087, 1409]]}, {"text": "% is the symbol for percent.", "conf": 0.891, "box": [[224, 1413], [647, 1425], [646, 1461], [223, 1450]]}, {"text": "Ratio", "conf": 0.725, "box": [[1086, 1425], [1164, 1425], [1164, 1460], [1086, 1460]]}, {"text": "A term used to compare two or more quantities of", "conf": 0.887, "box": [[208, 1468], [1003, 1489], [1002, 1529], [207, 1507]]}, {"text": "Antecedent", "conf": 0.848, "box": [[1087, 1474], [1249, 1480], [1248, 1511], [1086, 1504]]}, {"text": "the same kind is called \"Ratio\".", "conf": 0.909, "box": [[225, 1523], [692, 1537], [691, 1573], [224, 1559]]}, {"text": "Consequent", "conf": 0.831, "box": [[1089, 1523], [1255, 1529], [1254, 1563], [1088, 1557]]}, {"text": "The first term of the ratio is called the antecedent", "conf": 0.897, "box": [[196, 1578], [986, 1602], [985, 1638], [195, 1614]]}, {"text": "Continued ratio", "conf": 0.854, "box": [[1088, 1572], [1300, 1580], [1299, 1610], [1087, 1602]]}, {"text": "Rate", "conf": 0.796, "box": [[1086, 1620], [1154, 1624], [1152, 1657], [1084, 1653]]}, {"text": "and the second term is called the consequent.", "conf": 0.935, "box": [[224, 1634], [928, 1657], [926, 1695], [223, 1673]]}, {"text": "When two ratios x : y and y : z are expressed in the form of x : y : z, the ratio is", "conf": 0.9, "box": [[197, 1691], [1439, 1731], [1438, 1770], [196, 1729]]}, {"text": "called a continued ratio.", "conf": 0.871, "box": [[224, 1750], [588, 1760], [587, 1796], [223, 1786]]}, {"text": "A continued ratio is a comparison of three or more quantities in a certain order.", "conf": 0.941, "box": [[197, 1802], [1469, 1850], [1467, 1888], [196, 1841]]}, {"text": " A rate is a ratio that compares two quantities with different units of measure.", "conf": 0.912, "box": [[208, 1852], [1424, 1898], [1422, 1940], [206, 1894]]}, {"text": "90", "conf": 0.666, "box": [[785, 2005], [834, 2005], [834, 2042], [785, 2042]]}, {"text": "NOTFORSALE", "conf": 0.848, "box": [[1159, 2023], [1460, 2036], [1458, 2069], [1157, 2056]]}]}